# The laws a PGN record is replayed under (Sequence 28, Games: game rules are firmware; Sequence 27.1). They are
# decisions read from this file, never records: which variant a record's Variant tag names, and its law. A law governs
# which moves are legal and what a move does; it is in no position's ID, and the same position reached under two laws
# is one position. What a law adds to a position (pieces in hand, promoted pieces, checks given) is in the position,
# present only when there is any. Read by chess_rules.c (lp_chess_laws_load; LAPLACE_CHESS_FIRMWARE names another file).
#
#   variant NAME AXIS...       a variant a Variant tag can name, as the tag writes it ("Two Words" quoted; each way a
#                              source writes a name is its own line), and the axes of its law; an axis not said is
#                              Standard's:
#     castling standard | chess960 | none
#                              standard: the king castles from e with the rooks of a and h, and a FEN's KQkq name
#                              them. chess960: the king castles from wherever it starts with either rook it stands
#                              between, ending on g or c with the rook beside it on f or d (Chess960's rule, which
#                              holds standard's); a FEN's KQkq name the outermost rook on that side, a file letter
#                              (Shredder-FEN) that file's rook. none: no castling
#     drops                    a piece taken goes to its taker's hand (a promoted piece as a pawn) and is put from hand
#                              onto an empty square as a move (a pawn never onto the first or last rank)
#     explodes                 a capture removes the taker too and every piece but a pawn on the squares beside where
#                              it took; a king may not take, kings side by side give no check, and the game ends when a
#                              king is gone
#     captures forced          a side that can capture must
#     king unroyal             the king is a piece as any other: no check, no mate
#     king promotes            a pawn may become a king
#     pawns double first       a pawn on its side's first rank steps one or two
#     check forbidden          a move that gives check is not legal
#     checks N                 the game ends when a side has given N checks
#     goal SQUARE... [answered]
#                              the game ends when a king stands on one of these squares; answered: a White king there
#                              ends it only once Black's king cannot reach one with its move
#     start FEN                the position the variant starts from (quoted); else Standard's
#   default NAME               the variant of a record that names none (the PGN standard: standard chess)
#
# A record whose Variant no line here names is not replayed: its movetext is kept as its text and said.
default Standard
variant Standard castling standard
variant "From Position" castling standard
variant Chess960 castling chess960
variant Crazyhouse castling standard drops
variant "King of the Hill" castling standard goal d4 e4 d5 e5
variant Three-check castling standard checks 3
variant 3-check castling standard checks 3
variant Atomic castling standard explodes
variant Antichess castling none captures forced king unroyal king promotes
variant Horde castling standard pawns double first start "rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/1PP2PP1/PPPPPPPP/PPPPPPPP/PPPPPPPP/PPPPPPPP w kq - 0 1"
variant "Racing Kings" castling none check forbidden goal a8 b8 c8 d8 e8 f8 g8 h8 answered start "8/8/8/8/8/8/krbnNBRK/qrbnNBRQ w - - 0 1"
